  NOTE on (C).  Tao (Forum Math. Pi 2016, arXiv:1509.05422) proves the
  logarithmically averaged two-point Chowla conjecture
      sum_{x/w(x)<n<=x} lambda(a1 n+b1)lambda(a2 n+b2)/n = o(log w(x))
  for any fixed a1 b2 - a2 b1 != 0 and any w(x)->infinity; h=1 and h=2 both
  satisfy the determinant condition.  Taking w(x)=x gives sum_{n<=x} ll/n =
  o(log x), i.e. L(x) = o(1) -- UNCONDITIONAL.  The numerics above only
  confirm consistency on [1,10^8]; no finite computation proves o(1).
[PASS] C1.status :: (C) is an unconditional theorem in the literature (Tao 2016, arXiv:1509.05422, fixed shift, log-averaged), and its hypothesis (a1 b2 - a2 b1 != 0) does cover both h=1 and h=2
        hypothesis check: h=2 -> a=(1,0),b=(1,2), det = 1*2-1*0 = 2 != 0 ; h=1 -> det = 1*1-1*0 = 1 != 0.
        the theorem is a literature fact not re-derived here; L1-L5 verify the numerical signature on [1,10^8]

